{%- comment -%}
  AJ Join — the capture page ads point at.

  THE OFFER IS ACCESS, NOT A DISCOUNT. Every instinct says to put "10% off your
  first order" here, and this store cannot afford it: the Yoink is already
  clamped near cost and the Bargain Bin runs at a 20% margin floor, so another
  discount on top comes straight out of a contribution that is $12.67 on a median
  order. Early access costs nothing.

  AND IT PROMISES NO SEND FREQUENCY. An earlier version said "one email a day",
  which committed the business to a cadence nobody had decided on. The list is
  the asset; the schedule is a decision for later, and the copy should not have
  spent it in advance.

  IT ASKS FOR ONE THING. Every extra field costs conversion, and the whole point
  of the page is the email address — the business monetises on repeat visits, so
  the acquisition unit is a returning reader rather than a first order.

  Uses Shopify's own `customer` form, so a submission creates a customer
  subscribed to email marketing and lands in Shopify Email with nothing to
  maintain and nothing to pay for.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  `form` ONLY EXISTS INSIDE A `{% form %}` BLOCK, which is why the whole section
  is wrapped in one.

  It was read at the top of this file instead — outside any form — where it is
  nil, so `form.posted_successfully?` was ALWAYS false and the confirmation this
  section has carried since it was written had never once rendered. Signing up
  returned you to the same page showing the same empty form, which reads exactly
  like a submission that failed. Confirmed on the live page: requesting
  `/pages/join?customer_posted=true` returned no success markup at all.

  Wrapping is how Dawn does it and the only arrangement that works: the flag is
  scoped to the block, so the branch that reads it has to live inside the block.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign heading = section.settings.heading | default: 'Get first look at the good stuff'
-%}

<div
  class="aj-join color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} section spacing-style"
  style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
>
  {%- form 'customer', class: 'aj-join__wrap' -%}
  {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      THE CONFIRMATION IS ITS OWN PAGE, not a message where the form was.

      What was here before was one line and one link, inside the narrow card the
      email field had been sitting in — the layout still gave half the screen to
      a pitch aimed at somebody who had already said yes. This person is the
      most likely they will ever be to buy something: they have just handed over
      an address, they are still on the site, and they are holding a code. The
      page should spend its whole width on where to go next.

      THREE ROUTES, NAMED. "Shop now" is a sentence about us. "$175.20, gone at
      midnight" is a sentence about them, and each card carries the real product
      it points at rather than a category. A route with nothing behind it today
      renders nothing at all rather than a dead card promising a deal that is
      not there.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      # Resolved only once somebody has actually signed up, so the metaobject
      # walk is not paid for on every view of the form. The three routes are
      # named rather than generic — "shop now" is a sentence about us, "$175.20,
      # gone at midnight" is a sentence about them — so each needs its real
      # product. Same daily_deal walk as aj-daily-deal, aj-404, aj-cadence and
      # header-announcements: there is one definition of "today's Yoink" on this
      # store and this is not a second one.
      assign now_ts = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
      for entry in shop.metaobjects.daily_deal.values
        assign deal_starts = entry.starts_at.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
        assign deal_ends = entry.ends_at.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
        if deal_starts <= now_ts and deal_ends > now_ts
          assign deal_product = entry.product.value
          break
        endif
      endfor
      assign deal_variant = deal_product.selected_or_first_available_variant

      assign tee_collection = collections['tee-of-the-week']
      assign tee_product = tee_collection.products.first
      assign bin_collection = collections['bargain-bin']
    -%}

    <div class="page-width aj-join__done">
      <p class="aj-join__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.success_kicker | escape }}</p>
      <h1 class="aj-join__heading aj-join__heading--done">
        {{ section.settings.success_heading | escape }}
      </h1>
      <p class="aj-join__success">{{ section.settings.success_text | escape }}</p>

      {%- comment -%}
        ABOVE THE CARDS, AND NOT STYLED AS SMALL PRINT.

        This is the only line that says what the code is actually for, and it
        sat under three large cards at footnote size and 75% opacity — the
        cards take the clicks and the one instruction on the page gets skipped.
        Read in order it is also the answer to the line above it: "here's what
        it's for", then what it is for, then the three things that do not need
        it. Below the cards that sequence was broken in half.

        The setting id stays `success_fine` because the value is saved in
        page.join.json under that key; renaming it would orphan the copy.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.success_fine != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-join__done-note">{{ section.settings.success_fine | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <ul class="aj-join__routes" role="list">
        {%- if deal_product != blank -%}
          <li class="aj-join__route">
            <a class="aj-join__route-link" href="{{ deal_product.url }}">
              <span class="aj-join__route-label">Yoink of the Day</span>
              <span class="aj-join__route-title">{{ deal_product.title | escape }}</span>
              <span class="aj-join__route-fact">
                <span class="aj-join__route-price">{{ deal_variant.price | money }}</span>
                {%- if deal_variant.compare_at_price > deal_variant.price -%}
                  <s class="aj-join__route-was">{{ deal_variant.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="aj-join__route-go">Today only &rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if tee_product != blank -%}
          <li class="aj-join__route">
            <a class="aj-join__route-link" href="{{ tee_product.url }}">
              <span class="aj-join__route-label">Tee of the Week</span>
              <span class="aj-join__route-title">{{ tee_product.title | escape }}</span>
              <span class="aj-join__route-fact">
                <span class="aj-join__route-price">{{ tee_product.price | money }}</span>
                {%- if tee_product.compare_at_price > tee_product.price -%}
                  <s class="aj-join__route-was">{{ tee_product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="aj-join__route-go">Until Tuesday &rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if bin_collection != blank and bin_collection.products_count > 0 -%}
          <li class="aj-join__route">
            <a class="aj-join__route-link" href="{{ bin_collection.url }}">
              <span class="aj-join__route-label">The Bargain Bin</span>
              <span class="aj-join__route-title">{{ bin_collection.products_count }} things, all 25% off</span>
              {%- comment -%}
                NOT the price class. The Bin has no single price, and "Refilled
                every Thursday" set at price weight read as one — a $-sized
                sentence sitting exactly where the other two cards put a number.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <span class="aj-join__route-fact">
                <span class="aj-join__route-note">Refilled every Thursday</span>
              </span>
              <span class="aj-join__route-go">Have a dig &rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      </ul>

    </div>
  {%- else -%}
  <div class="page-width aj-join__inner">
    <div class="aj-join__copy">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-join__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <h1 class="aj-join__heading">{{ heading | escape }}</h1>

      {%- comment -%}
        THE OFFER, NAMED ON THE PAGE THE AD PROMISES IT ON.

        A new setting rather than edited copy, because heading and subheading are
        theme-editor values this file cannot reach — a default only renders while
        the setting is absent from the template JSON, which is exactly the case
        for a setting that did not exist until now.

        THE QUALIFIER IS NOT OPTIONAL. The signup code excludes
        `yoink-of-the-day`, `bargain-bin` and `tee-of-the-week` by tag, so "10%
        off" unqualified is false on the very products this store leads with.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.offer != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-join__offer">{{ section.settings.offer | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-join__subheading">{{ section.settings.subheading | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <ul class="aj-join__points" role="list">
        {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
          {%- assign key = 'point_' | append: i -%}
          {%- assign point = section.settings[key] -%}
          {%- if point != blank -%}
            <li class="aj-join__point">{{ point | escape }}</li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>

    </div>

    <div class="aj-join__form-col">
      {%- comment -%}
        THE CROW PERCHES ON THE CARD, which is why it sits in this column rather
        than under the copy. Its feet want to land on the card's top edge, so it
        is a sibling with a negative bottom margin rather than a background — a
        background would crop on narrow screens and there would be no way to keep
        the feet on the edge as the card grows.

        `aria-hidden` and an empty alt: it is decoration. A screen reader
        announcing "crow holding a diamond" before the email field would be
        noise in front of the one thing this page asks for.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.art != blank -%}
        <img
          class="aj-join__art"
          src="{{ section.settings.art | image_url: width: 520 }}"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          width="260"
          height="260"
          loading="lazy"
        >
      {%- endif -%}

    <div class="aj-join__form-card">
        {%- comment -%}
          A div, not a nested `{% form %}`. The section is wrapped in one so the
          confirmation can read `form.posted_successfully?`, and a form inside a
          form is invalid HTML that browsers silently drop — the inner fields
          would post to nothing.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="aj-join__form">
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="{{ section.settings.tag | escape }}">

          {%- if form.errors -%}
            <p class="aj-join__error">
              {{ form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize }}
              {{ form.errors.messages.email }}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}

          <label class="visually-hidden" for="aj-join-email">Email address</label>
          <input
            id="aj-join-email"
            class="aj-join__input"
            type="email"
            name="contact[email]"
            placeholder="you@example.com"
            autocomplete="email"
            required
          >

          <button class="aj-join__submit" type="submit">
            {{ section.settings.button_text | escape }}
          </button>

          {%- if section.settings.fine_print != blank -%}
            <p class="aj-join__fine">{{ section.settings.fine_print | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- endform -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .aj-join__inner {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--padding-lg, 2rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-join__inner { grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr; gap: var(--padding-xl, 3rem); }
  }

  .aj-join__heading { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .aj-join__subheading { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; opacity: 0.8; font-size: 1.05rem; }

  .aj-join__points { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }

  /* A drawn tick rather than a bullet: the list is three promises, and it should
     read as reassurance rather than as a table of contents. */
  .aj-join__point {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.6rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .aj-join__point::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.15rem;
    top: 0.45em;
    width: 0.55rem;
    height: 0.3rem;
    border-left: 2px solid currentColor;
    border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor;
    transform: rotate(-45deg);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .aj-join__form-card {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: var(--padding-lg, 2rem);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.04);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.1);
  }

  .aj-join__form { display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; }

  .aj-join__input {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.25);
    background: rgb(var(--color-background-rgb, 255 255 255));
    color: inherit;
  }

  .aj-join__submit {
    padding: 0.95rem 1rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    cursor: pointer;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb));
    color: rgb(var(--color-background-rgb, 255 255 255));
  }

  .aj-join__submit:hover { opacity: 0.9; }

  .aj-join__fine { margin: 0; font-size: 0.8125rem; opacity: 0.65; }
  .aj-join__error { margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #b3261e; }
  .aj-join__success { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; }

  .aj-join__cta {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb));
    color: rgb(var(--color-background-rgb, 255 255 255));
  }

  /*
    ON BRAND, 7 AUG 2026. This page was the only surface on the store that could
    have come from any Shopify theme — a white sheet, a black button, a system
    heading — while every other surface is teal, yellow or purple. It is also the
    page paid traffic points at, so it was the worst one to leave generic.

    THE PURPLE IS THE FOOTER'S PURPLE and the yellow is the price badge's yellow;
    nothing new is invented here. The heading takes Flashy at real scale for the
    reason aj-brand.css already documents — a display face needs room or it reads
    thin — and the eyebrow takes Ohpixel, which is the face this brand uses for
    short uppercase labels and the one that carries the 8-bit feel.
  */
  /*
    THE COLOUR GOES ON A CLASS THIS FILE OWNS, not on the section.

    The first attempt set it on `.aj-join` and shipped an UNREADABLE page: the
    background computed to `transparent` — the theme wins that property on the
    section element — while `color: #fff` applied fine, so every line of copy was
    white on white. Only the yellow eyebrow and ticks survived.

    Measured on the live page: `class="aj-join color- section"` — the colour
    scheme setting is EMPTY, so the theme's own scheme classes are malformed here
    and there is nothing to coordinate with. `.aj-join__inner` is defined in this
    file and targeted by nothing else, which makes it the one element whose
    background cannot be taken away.

    Background and text colour now live on the SAME element. They can no longer
    be separated, which is the actual bug — not the shade.
  */
  .aj-join__inner {
    background-color: #7a3fa0;
    color: #ffffff;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .aj-join__eyebrow {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }

  /*
    THE CONFIRMATION PANEL CARRIES ITS OWN COLOUR, for the reason documented
    above `.aj-join__inner`: the theme wins `background` on the section element,
    so background and text colour have to sit together on an element this file
    owns. `.aj-join__done` replaces `.aj-join__inner` entirely in this state
    rather than nesting inside it, so it has to repeat the pairing — splitting
    them is what once shipped white text on a white page.
  */
  .aj-join__done {
    background-color: #7a3fa0;
    color: #ffffff;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .aj-join__done .aj-join__heading--done {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    color: #fff;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .aj-join__done .aj-join__success {
    margin: 0 auto 0.5rem;
    max-width: 34ch;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    opacity: 0.92;
  }

  /*
    An instruction, not a disclaimer. Slightly quieter than the line above it
    because that one is the headline of the pair, but readable at body size and
    on the same measure — it is the sentence that tells somebody what they can
    do with the thing they were just given.
  */
  .aj-join__done-note {
    margin: 0 auto 2rem;
    max-width: 46ch;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .aj-join__routes {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    text-align: left;
  }

  /*
    AUTO-FIT RATHER THAN A FIXED THREE. Any of the three routes can be absent —
    the Bin empties, the tee sells out, there is a gap between Yoinks — and a
    hardcoded 3-column grid would leave a hole where the missing one was. This
    centres whatever survives.
  */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-join__routes { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr)); }
  }

  /* Same white slab as the form card, including the yellow top edge, because
     this is the same object doing the next job. */
  .aj-join__route-link {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    height: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    border-top: 4px solid var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    border-radius: 14px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 0.12s ease;
  }

  .aj-join__route-link:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }

  .aj-join__route-label {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    /* Purple on white, the same pairing the product page's eyebrow uses. */
    color: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
  }

  /* NOT Flashy. These are supplier product names — "Titan's Artisanal Mastery:
     Blue Galaxy Damascus Steel 5-Piece Kitchen Knife Set" — and a display face
     at that length stops being readable and starts being wallpaper. */
  .aj-join__route-title {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .aj-join__route-fact { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .aj-join__route-price { font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .aj-join__route-was { opacity: 0.55; font-size: 0.9375rem; }

  /* The fact slot when what fills it is a sentence rather than a number. */
  .aj-join__route-note { font-size: 0.9375rem; opacity: 0.75; }

  .aj-join__route-go {
    margin-top: auto;
    padding-top: 0.35rem;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }


  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__heading {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__subheading { color: #ffffff; opacity: 0.92; }
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__point { color: #ffffff; }
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__point::before { opacity: 1; color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000); }

  /* The card stays light: a form is the one thing here that should look like a
     form, and white on purple is the strongest contrast the palette offers. */
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__form-card {
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    border: 0;
    border-top: 4px solid var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }

  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__submit,
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__cta {
    background: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    border: 0;
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__submit:hover,
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__cta:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }

  /*
    THE CROW, AS A SETTING RATHER THAN A HARDCODED ASSET. The pixel art lives in
    Shopify Files, not in the theme, and a theme asset url carries a version hash
    that changes on every deploy. A picker also means the art can be swapped
    seasonally without a code change.

    `image-rendering: pixelated` is the whole point: without it the browser
    smooths 8-bit art on a high-DPI screen and it stops reading as pixel art.
  */
  /* The offer is the reason someone clicked, so it sits above the fold and
     takes the yellow — the same badge colour the storefront uses for a saving. */
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__offer {
    display: inline-block;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 1rem;
    background: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  /*
    PERCHED, NOT PLACED. The negative bottom margin is what puts the crow's feet
    on the card's top edge instead of leaving it hovering above a gap. It is
    tuned to the art's own transparent footer, so a different image will need a
    different number — which is the cost of a perch and worth it.

    `image-rendering: pixelated` is load-bearing: without it a browser smooths
    8-bit art on a high-DPI screen and it stops reading as pixel art.
  */
  .aj-join__form-col { position: relative; }

  .aj-join__art {
    display: block;
    width: 170px;
    height: auto;
    /*
      LEFT, NOT RIGHT. Parked in the right corner it read as decoration dropped
      into whitespace; over the card's leading edge it reads as a bird that has
      landed on the thing you are being asked to use. Same reason the overlap is
      generous rather than a touch — a 2px kiss looks like a mistake, an obvious
      overlap looks deliberate.
    */
    margin: 0 auto -22px 1.25rem;
    image-rendering: pixelated;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-join__art { width: 210px; margin-bottom: -28px; margin-left: 2rem; }
  }

  /*
    A HARD SHADOW, NOT A SOFT ONE. A blurred drop shadow under pixel art is the
    detail that makes the whole thing look accidental — the art has hard edges
    and the frame around it should too. Offset in ink, no blur, which is the
    same trick the 8-bit cards use.
  */
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__form-card {
    box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 rgba(40, 40, 40, 0.35);
  }

{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ Join",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "One a day, gone in 24 hours",
      "info": "Small pixel-face line above the heading. Uppercased automatically."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "offer",
      "label": "Offer line",
      "default": "Take 10% off your first order — full-price items, one use.",
      "info": "Must match what any ad pointing here promises. Leave blank to hide."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "art",
      "label": "Pixel art",
      "info": "The crow. Lives in Files rather than the theme so it can be swapped without a deploy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
